RF.put("questb:b2",{"8562":{"id":8562,"t":"Conqueror's Breastplate","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the the Carapace of the Old God, 2 Idols of War, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Honored reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nCarapace of the Old God C'Thun in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of War Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The unmentionable Old God slowly awakens from his slumber beneath Ahn'Qiraj. The terrible fate that awaits Azeroth could come in days or years; time has no meaning for beings of his power.\nWhen the stars are favorable, he will lash out against all living beings with terrible wrath. You must find him before then and find a way to bring his existence to an end.\nDo this and bring me a piece of his husk. I shall grant you armor no mortal has ever worn... armor fit for one who has slain a god!","rew":"You will receive:\nConqueror's Breastplate\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"At his dwelling in Ahn'Qiraj, dread C'Thun awaits in slumber.","done":"I did not expect you to return from your attempt, ‹name›.\nYou've fulfilled a destiny greater than that of most immortal beings.\nBy slaying C'Thun you've not only saved all of Azeroth, you've also tipped the scales of cosmic events beyond your comprehension.\nAccept this breastplate as a symbol of the glory and burden that will come as a consequence of your actions.\nMay its power aid you in the challenges that await you, god-slayer!\nStart Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Warrior Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8562\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Conqueror's Breastplate this quest\nBring the the Carapace of the Old God, 2 Idols of War, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nVethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8802":{"id":8802,"t":"The Savior of Kalimdor","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Eye of C'Thun to Anachronos at the Caverns of Time.\nEye of C'Thun C'Thun in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\nProvided: Eye of C'Thun","desc":"To the Caverns of Time you go, Lord/Lady ‹name›. Anachronos awaits your return. Give him the eye of C'Thun as he will undoubtedly wish to place it in his master's collection.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAmulet of the Fallen God Cloak of the Fallen God Ring of the Fallen God\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Lord ‹name›! It is over...","done":"The Master has left these for you, champion. From the timeless cache: A collection of artifacts spanning thousands of years - the choice is yours.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"7282":{"id":7282,"t":"Brotherly Love","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel into Frostwolf territory and slay Commander Louis Philips. Return to Commander Karl Philips when the task is complete.\nCommander Louis Philips slain","desc":"He must be put out of his misery, soldier! He knows not what he does. He has become a mindless servant of the dreaded Banshee Queen.\nVenture forth, across the Field of Strife, to the depths of Frostwolf territory. Find my brother and destroy him. His torment must come to an end.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"It is with heavy heart that I give such an order, soldier.","done":"You did remember to burn the corpse, didn't you?\nStart Commander Karl Philips Alterac Valley End Commander Karl Philips Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Both factions Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 7282","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7122":{"id":7122,"t":"Capture a Mine","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 90s instead of 0.","obj":"Capture a mine that the Stormpike does not control, then return to Sergeant Durgen Stormpike in the Alterac Mountains.\nMine Captured","desc":"The mines in Alterac Valley hold more than just minerals. Both the Frostwolf and Stormpike have cached excess supplies in the Irondeep and Coldtooth mines... that's not a bad idea, if we could only maintain control of them!\nCapture a mine, then return to me. To capture a mine, enter one that we do not control and kill its leader. When you do that, the mine will be ours, and we'll send troops to protect it!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"You haven't captured the mine yet, ‹name›!\nAfter we control a mine, it will be much easier to gather minerals and supplies from it.","done":"You did it! Well done, ‹name›!\nWhen we control a mine and have troops stationed there, it's much easier to gather minerals and supplies from it.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":36.8,"y":77.2,"n":"Sergeant Durgen Stormpike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7202":{"id":7202,"t":"Korrak the Bloodrager","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 14,300, 0.7 times as much.","obj":"According to legend, the leader of the mighty Winterax trolls appears at will to wreak havoc on the denizens of Alterac Valley.\nShould Korrak make himself known, destroy him and return to Lieutenant Haggerdin in the Alterac Mountains.\nKorrak the Bloodrager slain","desc":"The indigenous Winterax trolls of the region are ruthless savages that would love nothing more than to have our bones added to their foul stew.\nWe must show them our might!\nWe have recovered tomes from their caves that detail their leadership hierarchy. The artifacts indicate that their leader, Korrak the Bloodrager, tends to remain hidden until given a reason to make his presence known.\nDeath to Korrak would mean death to Winterax Clan! Slay him and return.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBloodseeker Ice Barbed Spear Wand of Biting Cold\nYou will also receive:\nRune of Recall\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Lieutenant Haggerdin","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"8162":{"id":8162,"t":"Cut Arathor Supply Lines","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Deathstalker Mortis at Hammerfall.\nArathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"The League of Arathor is sparing no expense in their move to retake Arathi. They, and all the races of the Alliance, now stream to this distant region, intent on expanding their hold from Refuge Pointe. We must stop them, and the best means to stop them is to take their supplies.\nYou can help us, ‹name›. Enter Arathi Basin, known for its rich mines, fertile land and skilled craftsman. Capture and control every base you can, win the battle, and return to me with the resources you gain.","rew":"Money: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,000\n+200 reputation with The Defilers\nLevel 25 , requires level 20 Difficulty 20 21 23 28 33 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable No Quest ID 8162","cats":["arathi-basin"]},"642":{"id":642,"t":"The Princess Trapped","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 12 Motes of Myzrael, then bring them to the Iridescent Shards in Drywhisker Gorge.\n12 Mote of Myzrael Drywhisker Digger 50 % , Drywhisker Surveyor 50 % , Drywhisker Kobold 50 %","desc":"My name is Myzrael. I am a princess of the earth, and my captors, the giants, have trapped me deep beneath the Arathi Highlands. These crystal shards are the only way I can speak with the surface world.\nPlease help me. Allies of the giants, the Drywhisker Kobolds, have a shard like this one in their Drywhisker Gorge, to the east. To power the cluster, you must gather Motes of Myzrael from the kobolds and apply them to it.\nI beg you, ‹name›, aid me!","rew":"Experience: 2,850","back":"This cluster of shards looks much like the Shards of Myzrael. But the same feeling of security does not pulse through them.","done":"Ah! You activated these shards. Already I feel more myself!\nBut alas, I am still far from free...","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":62.5,"y":33.7,"n":"Shards of Myzrael","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":84.3,"y":31,"n":"Iridescent Shards","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"6482":{"id":6482,"t":"Freedom to Ruul","lv":24,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Ruul, then speak with Yama Snowhoof in Splintertree Post.","desc":"Eh? Who are you?\n‹name›? You're no furbolg. They are cursed! They thought I was a bear and captured me, and now they starve me! My strength is failing...\nHelp me escape, then speak with my sister Yama at the Splintertree Post to the east.\n‹name›! I must escape!","rew":"Money: 17 0 gold, 17 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,400\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Have you seen my brother Ruul? He walked into the forest days ago and has not returned...","done":"You found my brother! He was captured by the Thistlefurs? That is terrible news to hear, for although many Furbolgs are noble creatures, the Thistlefurs are corrupt.\nThank you for rescuing my brother, ‹name›. I do not want to think of how they treated poor Ruul. He will likely sleep long after this ordeal...","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":41.5,"y":34.5,"n":"Ruul Snowhoof","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":74.1,"y":60.9,"n":"Yama Snowhoof","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"2":{"id":2,"t":"Sharptalon's Claw","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Sharptalon's Claw to Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.\nSharptalon's Claw Sharptalon\nProvided: Sharptalon's Claw","desc":"The mighty hippogryph Sharptalon has been slain, with the claw of the felled beast serving as a testament to your victory. Senani Thunderheart at the Splintertree Post will no doubt be interested in seeing this trophy as proof of your deeds.","rew":"Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Yes, mighty ‹class›, I sensed your arrival. I trust you have more news to report to me about your hunt?","done":"Most impressive, ‹name›... the claw of Sharptalon could not have been easy to get! The Ashenvale Hunt goes well for you!\nSharptalon had long terrorized the peons from the lumber camps near its path as they tried to travel here to Splintertree Post. No doubt once the word gets out that it was you who put down the beast, many rousing songs of your bravery will be heard at campfires and lumber mills across Ashenvale!","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":73.8,"y":61.5,"n":"Senani Thunderheart","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"1042":{"id":1042,"t":"The Carevin Family","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Jonathan Carevin in Darkshire.","desc":"No, I don't have any records of a Velinde Starsong staying in Darkshire... though, if you don't mind me saying, I can hardly imagine a night elf priestess taking a room in the inn, if you get my meaning?\nThese wolf-men you mentioned though, that's something I've heard about. Just the other day, Calor came into town with a string of their heads. He works with the Carevin family. Hunters of demons, undead, and other monstrosities. Speak with Jonathan, he's the head of the household.","rew":"Experience: 250","done":"Dark times these are. Ill news is whispered from every swaying branch, and evil can be found under every rock.\nAnd in such times an unknown stranger enters my home and asks of worgen... I'll ask no forgiveness for my suspicions, only answers.\nAnd answers, I will have.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.5,"y":46.9,"n":"Clerk Daltry","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.3,"y":49,"n":"Jonathan Carevin","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3602":{"id":3602,"t":"Azsharite","lv":58,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Recover twenty Crystallized Azsharite from southern Azshara. You may use the Felhound to assist you in 'sniffing' out the location of cleverly hidden deposits.\nReturn to Loramus when the task is complete.\n20 Crystallized Azsharite Azsharite Formation , Azsharite Formation , Azsharite Formation , Azsharite Formation\nProvided: Felhound Tracker Kit","desc":"The ancient cliff giants of the southern region of Azshara consume the rock and buildings of the land for sustenance. The excrement from their consumption is a highly malleable and extremely strong crystal known as Azsharite.\nThe formations litter the southern arc, but few are ever recovered due to the extremely violent nature of the giants.\nYou are to venture south and recover enough of the Azsharite for the creation of the weapon's body. My felhounds will aid in the recovery of the crystal.","rew":"Money: 2 65 2 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,750","back":"Evil does not sleep, fool. You will have time for rest when you are finally dead. Now, bring me those crystals.","done":"Your tasks in Azshara are complete, mortal. I must now forge the necessary components for the next step in your adventure.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":60.8,"y":66.4,"n":"Loramus Thalipedes","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"6562":{"id":6562,"t":"Trouble in the Deeps","lv":22,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.","desc":"Je'neu Sancrea is in need of aid. He is at the Zoram'gar Outpost in Ashenvale. The Night elf forest is to the north of the Stonetalon mountains. You can reach it by traveling through Windshear Crag or by heading north through Barrens. Zoram Strand is far to the west of the forest. Be careful, ‹name›. There are forces there that will not take to your presence kindly.","rew":"Experience: 440\n+25 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+100 reputation with Earthen Ring","done":"Tsunaman sent you? Excellent. Then we have matters to discuss.\nStonetalon Mountains Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":47.4,"y":64.2,"n":"Tsunaman","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":11.6,"y":34.3,"n":"Je'neu Sancrea","e":1}],"cats":["blackfathom-deeps"]},"4242":{"id":4242,"t":"Abandoned Hope","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Marshal Maxwell the bad news.","desc":"Bolvar is a fool. I was gathering his precious 'proof' so that I could shove it down his throat.\nHe is a blind buffoon. Proof stands two feet away from him and he does not see.\nAs for my data, it's lost. Gone. Unrecoverable.\nShould I ever find Ironfoe and make it out of this labyrinth, my first stop will be Stormwind, to place my hammer in between that reptile's eyes.\nLeave me, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nConservator Helm Shieldplate Sabatons Windshear Leggings\nExperience: 5,450\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","done":"He's gone mad, apparently.\n<Maxwell lowers his head in mourning.>\nIt is unfortunate that a once proud and noble warrior would be turned into a blithering head case. I GUESS we've reached a dead end...\nI must reward you for your efforts thus far, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.7,"y":69,"n":"Marshal Maxwell","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4082":{"id":4082,"t":"KILL ON SIGHT: High Ranking Dark Iron Officials","lv":54,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture to Blackrock Depths and destroy the vile aggressors!\nWarlord Goretooth wants you to kill 10 Anvilrage Medics, 10 Anvilrage Soldiers and 10 Anvilrage Officers. Return to him once your task is complete.\nAnvilrage Medic slain : 0/ 10\nAnvilrage Soldier slain : 0/ 10\nAnvilrage Officer slain : 0/ 10","desc":"By order of Warlord Goretooth, commander of the Kargath Expeditionary Force:\nHead of the K.E.F. reconnaissance division, Grandmaster Lexlort, has returned with news of the whereabouts of high ranking Dark Iron officials. Through locked gate, near the heart of the city, they train their forces to snuff out our men. Travel to Blackrock Depths and destroy them!\nCompletion of this mission will result in a tribute.","rew":"Money: 1 65 1 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,450\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"You again? I have to hand it to you, ‹name›, you are tenacious.","done":"Angerforge is undoubtedly... angry. Return to me when you receive a third tribute and we shall proceed with Operation: Death to Angerforge. I cannot go into any detail of what this entails, but rest assured, it involves somebody dying.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":3.9,"y":46.7,"n":"KILL ON SIGHT","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":5.8,"y":47.5,"n":"Warlord Goretooth","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4002":{"id":4002,"t":"The Eastern Kingdom","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from The Eastern Kingdom.","obj":"Speak with Thrall if you are prepared to take on the mission he has planned.","desc":"You bring excellent information, ‹name›.\nAs Warchief, it is my duty to do what is best for the Horde. To ensure that the generations that come after us are not forced into a hopeless existence.\nThe opportunity to shape our future alliances has fallen into our collective laps. A move to help the dwarves could greatly strengthen our relationships in the Eastern Kingdoms. This, then, is why you must not fail!\nAre you prepared?","done":"There is no going back beyond this point, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4322":{"id":4322,"t":"Jail Break!","lv":58,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Help Marshal Windsor get his gear back and free his friends. Return to Marshal Maxwell if you succeed.","desc":"We need to get out of here, ‹name›. Help me get my gear back from the supply area and free my friends. If we make it out of here, you are to proceed to Morgan's Vigil and speak with Marshal Maxwell. He will give you further instruction.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBlade of Reckoning Skilled Fighting Blade\nYou will also receive:\nWard of the Elements\nMoney: 1 75 1 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,750\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You look exhausted, ‹name›. Perhaps you should have a seat by the fire and relax.","done":"Amazing, ‹name›. Simply amazing. Windsor stormed through here not five minutes ago. He makes some grand claims but purports that they are supported by his evidence. He is on his way to Stormwind now to confront Bolvar and ... Lady Prestor.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.7,"y":69,"n":"Marshal Maxwell","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"8962":{"id":8962,"t":"Components of Importance","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire Druidical Remains and return them to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.\nDruidical Remains Hive'Regal Ambusher , Hive'Regal Burrower , Hive'Regal Spitfire , Hive'Regal Slavemaker and 1 more","desc":"‹class›, listen closely. Now that we have the brazier, and the means to light it, we still need another component to suffuse it with; something that will provide a focus strong enough to entice the spirit of my deceased, former comrade.\nMor Grayhoof, our most prominent druid, had many close friends amongst the Cenarion Circle, some of which have fallen to the silithid. I need you to retrieve some Druidical Remains from the silithid that inhabit the environs of Hive'Regal in southeastern Silithus.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Have you returned already then, ‹class›, with what I sent you out to gather?","done":"A job well done, ‹name›. I will imbue the essence of the remains into the brazier.\nNow all that is left is to go to the lower portion of Blackrock Spire, to the chamber where War Master Voone resides in Tazz'Alaor, and use the brazier to summon forth the corrupted spirit of my former cohort, Mor Grayhoof. He cannot rest until the amulet piece is taken from him.\nBurning Steppes Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"4482":{"id":4482,"t":"Libram of Tenacity","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -30g instead of 0.","obj":"Black Diamond Borer Beetle 5.2 % , Dark Keeper Uggel 4.6 % , Crest Killer 3.8 % , Burrowing Thundersnout 3.6 % and 4 more\nLibram of Tenacity Irondeep Explorer 1.3 % in Alterac Valley , Blackrock Ambusher 0.4 % , Coldmine Miner 0.3 % in Alterac Valley , Hakkari Oracle 0.2 % and 4 more\n4 Crystal Ward\nEye of Kajal","rew":"You will receive:\nLesser Arcanum of Tenacity","back":"Thirty gold, ‹race›. Thirty gold and the required components.","done":"It took Kariel what would amount to several of your lifetimes to complete the libram that you now hold, ‹race›. All for what? So that his disciple could stand in the Burning Steppes and bastardize his research in order to satiate a never ending arcane craving... Curse this foul addiction.\nI am disgusted with your lack of compassion and insatiable greed. Be gone!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65,"y":23.6,"n":"Mathredis Firestar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"5522":{"id":5522,"t":"Leonid Barthalomew","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Frozen Eggs to Leonid Barthalomew in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nFrozen Eggs\nProvided: Frozen Eggs","desc":"I received a message from my master, Vectus. Well, the message wasn't really from Vectus...it was from someone named Leonid Barthalomew. I don't know Leonid, but he knew my master, and no one knows my master unless he allows it.\nLeonid says Vectus wants the dragon eggs. He wants you to deliver them to him at the Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nThat hurts! Why you? Doesn't Vectus trust me? Oh, never mind... just take the eggs and tell Leonid that I did what our master commanded.","rew":"Experience: 4,950\n+75 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You are the one up to mischief in Blackrock Spire, yes? Do you have what I asked for?","done":"Ah, very good. You do not know the evil power for whom you have labored, but now you will know the truth. And fear not--I am no servant of that master. I am Leonid Barthalomew, known as \"the Revered\" to my brethren in the Argent Dawn.\nI tricked Tinkee into sending you and the dragon eggs to me. And it is good that my trick was successful, for had these eggs reached their intended destination, a great power would have fallen into the hands of the enemy.\nBurning Steppes Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65.2,"y":24,"n":"Tinkee Steamboil","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.9,"y":48.3,"n":"Leonid Barthalomew the Revered","e":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97922":{"id":97922,"t":"Camping 101 leatherworking","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Adele Fielder in Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your leatherworking skill to 20","desc":"You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, ‹class›. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.","done":"There you have it, your very own camp tent. Most folk don't care much for tents being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.8,"y":63.2,"n":"Sam Sarsaparilla","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":46.4,"y":62.2,"n":"Adele Fielder","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94322":{"id":94322,"t":"Craftsmans writ limited invulnerability potion","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Limited Invulnerability Potion\nLimited Invulnerability Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Limited Invulnerability Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Limited Invulnerability Potion Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94322","cats":["crafting"]},"94242":{"id":94242,"t":"Craftsmans writ pilferers gloves","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Pilferer's Gloves\nPilferer's Gloves","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Pilferer's Gloves, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Pilferer's Gloves Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94242","cats":["crafting"]},"4722":{"id":4722,"t":"Beached Sea Turtle","lv":13,"min":11,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Sea Turtle Remains to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.\nSea Turtle Remains Skeletal Sea Turtle\nProvided: Sea Turtle Remains","desc":"You find a corpse of a sea turtle that had beached itself on the coast of Darkshore some time ago. It has been scavenged by the murlocs who have encamped themselves around the creature's remains. Still, there appear to be some suitable samples left on the creature's remains that Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine might be able to make use of.","rew":"Money: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 460\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello ‹name› - do you have any discoveries of creatures that have washed ashore to report on?","done":"Another discovery for us to research - well done ‹name›! These remains will be properly studied once they get to Darnassus. Please accept this small honorarium in exchange for the remains you have provided for our study.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.1,"y":62.2,"n":"Beached Sea Turtle","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.6,"y":45.6,"n":"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"1362":{"id":1362,"t":"The Kolkar of Desolace","lv":32,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Felgur Twocuts at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace.","desc":"The Kolkar centaur live in Desolace, and their forces have spread into the Barrens. This is a known fact and we have Horde agents dealing with them here.\nBut as long as the centaur are strong in Desolace, they will always pose a threat. It is time we rid ourselves of that threat.\nSpeak with Felgur Twocuts at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace. He was sent to gather intelligence on the centaur. He will know how to best deal with the Kolkar of Desolace.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"You are here on orders from Regthar? Then you are here to deal with the centaur. Good.\nI hope you're rested. I don't know how our campaign against the centaur will end, but I know the struggle will be long.\nHave a seat, and listen.\nThe Barrens Desolace","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":45.3,"y":28.4,"n":"Regthar Deathgate","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":56.2,"y":59.6,"n":"Felgur Twocuts","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"6002":{"id":6002,"t":"Body and Heart","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Cenarion Lunardust on the Moonkin Stone between Mulgore and the Barrens to bring forth Lunaclaw. From there, you must face Lunaclaw and earn the strength of body and heart it possesses.\nSpeak with Turak Runetotem in Thunder Bluff when you are done.\nProvided: Cenarion Lunardust","desc":"On land west of Taurajo in the Barrens - just before it turns into Mulgore - lies a Moonkin Stone. The moonkin are special beasts, not native to these parts. Lunaclaw, the stone's defender, will face you when Cenarion Lunardust is applied to it. Lunaclaw possesses within it a strength that you must use as one of the Claw.\nYou've earned the right to use this Cenarion Lunardust, ‹name›... now show me that you've earned the right to possess the strength of body and the strength of heart needed as a druid!","rew":"Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"You have finally taken your large step into a much larger world, ‹name›. I sense the teaching of the Great Bear Spirit within you, and I sense that you have received the strength that Lunaclaw possessed.\nThere are no further obstacles in your way... let me now teach you what it means to be a Druid of the Claw!\nThunder Bluff The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Turak Runetotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"5922":{"id":5922,"t":"Moonglade","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the spell \"Teleport: Moonglade\" to travel to Moonglade. When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.","desc":"All druids are welcomed to the sacred lands of Moonglade, tauren and night elf alike. Keeper Remulos - Moonglade's guardian - keeps watch over all druids who hibernate there. Now that you're learning the ways of the Claw, I'll teach you the spell that lets you transport yourself there. Cast it whenever you seek Moonglade's knowledge or solace.\nAs for your first lesson, travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you're now on. Good luck, young druid.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"\"And so it begins. Father Cenarius. And so it begins.\"\nDendrite makes a quick, invisible gesture in the air above him. A slight aura of power falls over him.\n\"The first perspective of nature you must adapt to is that of the bear. I will put you on the path to understanding this aspect of druidic life, but it is you that must embrace it and propagate it - now and forever!\"\nThunder Bluff Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Turak Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"98322":{"id":98322,"t":"Secure the mountain","lv":8,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Check in on Mountaineer Gretchen west of Kharanos.","desc":"Spelunking dark caves is adventurer business. My job's just to make reports and send them over to Ironforge.\nTrouble is, one of my reports hasn't... well, reported back. I asked a few mountaineers to learn more about the wendigo problem we have out here, but I haven't heard from them.\nIf you're already going to be out and about, what say you don't check in with Mountaineer Gretchen just west of town. I'm late enough as it is!","done":"Ol' Whitebeard sent ya, aye?\nI got his report, alright. This whole situation's a mess!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.6,"y":53.8,"n":"Senir Whitebeard","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":44,"y":57,"n":"Mountaineer Gretchen","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"4402":{"id":4402,"t":"Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Mining for Dummies, Wild Harvest, Pelt Collecting for Beginners.","obj":"Bring Galgar 10 Cactus Apples. You remember him saying that they could be found near cactuses.\n10 Cactus Apple Cactus Apple","desc":"It sure gets hot out here in the Valley of Trials.\n<Galgar wipes his brow.>\nIf only I had some cactus apples, I could make my famous cactus apple surprise! Nothing cools you off faster than a piece of that delicious treat.\nI'll tell you what, ‹name›. If you bring me 10 cactus apples, I'll make you a few portions of cactus apple surprise to take with you on your adventures, and a free training manual, too. If you're interested, you can find cactus apples growing near the cactus plants around here.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMining for Dummies Wild Harvest Pelt Collecting for Beginners\nNew in Forever: Mining for Dummies, Wild Harvest, Pelt Collecting for Beginners.\nYou will also receive:\n10 Cactus Apple Surprise\nMoney: 50 0 gold, 0 silver, 50 copper Experience: 380\n+200 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+200 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Have you finished collecting cactus apples?","done":"Wonderful, ‹name›! As promised, here is your cactus apple surprise plus a little something extra.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.7,"y":67.2,"n":"Galgar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"97282":{"id":97282,"t":"Stormy potential","lv":11,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 5 Charged Thunder Lizard Organs to Rezlak near Drygulch Ravine.\n5 Charged Thunder Lizard Organ","desc":"\"Rezlack, when an opportunity come's knocking make sure you're ready to seize it.\" That's another gem Gazlowe taught me and that's exactly what I intend to do.\nThis orb doesn't seem damaged, it just looks like it's out of juice, but I've the idea to supercharge it back to full strength!\nThere are a bunch of thunder lizards in a gorge west of here. They have organs that hold a strong electrical charge that would be perfect for this.\nGo harvest some and bring them back to me!","rew":"You will receive:\nMakeshift Stormcaller\nMoney: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 875\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"It might come as a surprise that with a name like thunder lizard they shoot lightning instead of roaring like thunder.\nWell, they do. Shoot lightning, I mean.\nTrust me, it's a lesson you only get to learn once if you're lucky.","done":"Hey, thanks pal! You've been a really big help to me here and I appreciate it.\nHere's to hoping I can get this all charged up using these organs. I bet it'll make those no good harpies think twice about attacking my caravan again. I sure hope this works.\nEither way you've done your side of the deal. Take this for your trouble.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":46.4,"y":23,"n":"Rezlak","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"79362":{"id":79362,"t":"Grants shield","lv":25,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Grant's Mace on one of the skeletons in Raven Hill Cemetery then return to Sirra Von'Indie in Darkshire for more information.\nGrant's Mace\nProvided: Grant's Shield","desc":"A shield left behind by the specter of Grant Valor, father of the Valor family and hero of Raven Hill.\nWith Grant's spirit still battling the undead, perhaps his unfinished business was to slay the scourge that injured him in the Raven Hill Cemetery. It is likely the one his mace is still imbedded in.","back":"You' legs be lookin' a wobbly der. De ground be shakin?","done":"Let's get ready to rumble, ya?\nAlterac Mountains Duskwood","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":80.4,"y":66.8,"n":"Bath'rah the Windwatcher","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"322":{"id":322,"t":"Blessed Arm","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Crate of Lightforge Ingots to Grimand Elmore in Stormwind.\nCrate of Lightforge Ingots\nProvided: Crate of Lightforge Ingots","desc":"There is a dwarven weaponsmith in the Dwarven District of Stormwind who can craft with lightforge iron. His name is Grimand Elmore.\nI've packed the iron you found into a crate. Take it to Grimand and tell him your tale. I'm sure he'll oblige someone on a quest such as yours, and craft for you a weapon - a weapon to give even Morbent Fel worry!","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","back":"How might I ply my craft for you, ‹class›?","done":"That is quite a tale you have. And lightforge iron! Not for years have I worked with such a metal. It will be an honor to craft with it again. And you must return to me later with the story of your battle against the Necromancer.\nBut we get ahead of ourselves. First, your weapon against Morbent Fel...\nWetlands Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.6,"y":60.6,"n":"Glorin Steelbrow","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":59.7,"y":33.8,"n":"Grimand Elmore","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1202":{"id":1202,"t":"The Theramore Docks","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Captain's Documents to Nazeer Bloodpike in Brackenwall Village.\nCaptain's Documents Captain's Footlocker","desc":"‹name›, two of our spies were sent to steal documents from a ship at the Theramore docks. They gained the papers but were discovered, and were forced to throw the documents into the sea.\nOne spy later escaped, but was unable to recover the prize. He reported his failure to me, and I now charge the task to you.\nThe documents are in a footlocker, in the waters somewhere beneath the Theramore docks. Find those documents, ‹name›, and bring them to me.","rew":"Experience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Did you find the documents, ‹name›? They hold information vital to the stability of the Alliance and, hence, vital to the security of the Horde.","done":"I commend you, ‹name›. This was not an easy mission. But the documents you gained are valued greatly by our superiors.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":35.2,"y":30.7,"n":"Nazeer Bloodpike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"1282":{"id":1282,"t":"They Call Him Smiling Jim","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Captain Garran Vimes on the top floor of Foothold Citadel.","desc":"I can't help it if I feel sorry for ol' Jim there. He wasn't always like that. Ran an inn out in the marsh for a while, wonderful place.\nLook, I don't really want to talk about it. Bring it up with Captain Vimes if you really have to. He's stationed on the top floor of Foothold Citadel, the large barracks to the east of Lady Jaina's tower.","rew":"Experience: 280","done":"James Hyal's his real name. He opened an inn at the edge of the Barrens. Wanted to make a nice place for travelers to stop over...\nMight be he was thinking too big, but the inn did do well for a while. Then we lost control of the roads in the marsh, and the ogres took over.\nJames was too stubborn to give up his dream for safety within our walls, and the Shady Rest Inn was burnt to the ground. We're investigating, but haven't had much luck. If you want to help out, see what you can find in the rubble.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":66.2,"y":46.1,"n":"Guard Byron","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68.2,"y":48.6,"n":"Captain Garran Vimes","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"9202":{"id":9202,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Major Healing Potion","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 20 Major Healing Potions and the Craftsman's Writ - Major Healing Potion - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Major Healing Potion\n20 Major Healing Potion Quartermaster Zigris , Muigin 40 % , Imperial Qiraji Destroyer 30 % , Colossal Anubisath Warbringer 30 % and 4 more\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Major Healing Potion","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order AL-169110:\n20 Major Healing Potions.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"Do you know what the troops on the front lines call these? Priests in a bottle...\n<Packmaster Stonebruiser sings.>\n\"I'm your priest in a bott-le baby... you gotta drink me the right way...\"\nWhat's the matter sonny? It's a very popular song around these parts.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9122":{"id":9122,"t":"The Dread Citadel - Naxxramas","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -30g instead of 0.","obj":"Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 2 Arcane Crystals, 1 Nexus Crystal and 30 gold pieces. You must also be Revered with the Argent Dawn.\n2 Arcane Crystal Hakkari Thorium Vein 5.8 % , Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Ooze Covered Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Small Thorium Vein 2.6 % and 4 more\nNexus Crystal\nReach 21000 reputation with Argent Dawn","desc":"In the thick of Plaguewood lies the entrance to the dread citadel of Naxxramas. Previously, all attempts to enter had been stymied by the magical wards placed upon the rune portal. That is, until now.\nWe have devised a way to gain entry via a permanent arcane cloaking of sorts - an old cantrip of the Kirin Tor with a few modifications of my own. With that said, the cloaking is costly. Since your dedication to the cause of the Dawn is admirable, we are willing to incur some of those costs.","rew":"+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"None have entered Naxxramas and lived to tell the tale.","done":"You will feel a slight tingle, ‹name›. That sensation means it's working. Once complete, you will be able to enter Naxxramas by stepping upon the rune portal in Plaguewood.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.7,"n":"Archmage Angela Dosantos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"95682":{"id":95682,"t":"Open the maw","lv":31,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay the Dragonmaw forces within the Excavation Site and return to the Deathstalker Agent outside with anything you recover.\nDragonmaw Saboteur slain : 0/ 2\nDragonmaw Warder slain : 0/ 4\nDragonmaw Dispatch","desc":"Dragonmaw. <She lets out a dry, amused scoff.>\nThe remnants of the dragon-wrangling clan think they've found something that could lead to them rising to their former power. In the eyes of whom... their false warchief?\nClear out their ragtag clan within the Excavation Sites so our Deathstalkers can move in undetected.\nIf the Dragonmaw carry anything of note upon them, return it to me--this information must stay between us and our royal command.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nKnife-Polishing Rag Dirt-Heavy Bracers\nYou will also receive:\nBloody Map\nExperience: 6,950","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":51.4,"y":59.2,"n":"Deathstalker Agent","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["excavation-site-wetlands-dungeon"]},"6162":{"id":6162,"t":"A Husband's Last Battle","lv":51,"min":46,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Overlord Ror and return his claw to Dreka'Sur at Bloodvenom Post in Felwood.\nOverlord Ror's Claw Overlord Ror","desc":"My husband traveled Felwood for the honor of our clan, doing battle against the Shadow Council and other corrupt atrocities!\nAfter he escaped death numerous times, I received a letter from him saying that a druid asked him for help against a great befouled furbolg named Overlord Ror--the two were never heard from again.\nI want this Ror's clawed hand, ‹name›. I want it to pay for leaving me a widow! I believe the creature is to the south... near the Ashenvale border.","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,900\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Do you have the beast's claw yet, ‹name›? It will pay for its crimes. I don't care if it's corrupt or just angry for living in such a dismal forest. No furbolg will live for long committing such crimes against my family!","done":"You bring honor to me for following through with your word. My husband died in battle--he would have been proud of that. But I could not rest until I knew that the creature that has forced me to live my life alone paid for what it had done.\nThank you again, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":34.8,"y":52.7,"n":"Dreka'Sur","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"5202":{"id":5202,"t":"A Strange Red Key","lv":55,"min":49,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search through Jaedenar to discover what the Blood Red Key is used for.\nBlood Red Key Jaedenar Darkweaver 3.6 % , Jaedenar Warlock 3.5 % , Jaedenar Enforcer 3.5 % , Ulathek 3 % and 1 more\nProvided: Blood Red Key","desc":"The small red key seems to be made of some kind of bone material. It is heavy in your hand, but appears very fragile. Why would a member of the Shadow Council have such a thing? Perhaps there is something within Jaedenar that this strange key unlocks.","rew":"Experience: 5,650","back":"I begin to wonder if I'll ever escape this cage.\nIt's only a matter of time before they sacrifice me to whatever demons they worship. The monsters!","done":"The key, you've found it! Please, give it to me and I can finally escape!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":36.2,"y":55.5,"n":"Captured Arko'narin","e":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"3122":{"id":3122,"t":"Return to Witch Doctor Uzer'i","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Neeru's Herb Pouch to Witch Doctor Uzer'i in Feralas.\nNeeru's Herb Pouch\nProvided: Neeru's Herb Pouch","desc":"Here are the herbs, ‹name›. Take them to Witch Doctor Uzer'i.\nPlease let him know that I am satisfied with the shrunken head.","rew":"Experience: 975\n+25 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Have you spoken to Neeru?","done":"This is just what I need to prepare the muisek vessel, ‹name›. Soon we will see if my latest incantations prove to be as powerful as I had hoped.\nPlease, a moment. I must perform the ritual and apply the herbs.\nOrgrimmar Feralas","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":49.5,"y":50.6,"n":"Neeru Fireblade","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Witch Doctor Uzer'i","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"3842":{"id":3842,"t":"A Short Incubation","lv":47,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Elixir of Fortitudes to Quentin in Thousand Needles.\n2 Elixir of Lesser Fortitude","desc":"The Moonweavers, huh? Most intriguing. I wish the sprite darters could truly appreciate what it means to have those two look after them. They are both quite capable.\nSo, they gave you the egg as a gift. Well, then you should be responsible for it for as long as you desire. It appears it's almost ready to hatch, but we should ensure it's healthy and no damage has been done to it.\nI only need two elixirs of fortitude for a small spell to protect the egg. I have the rest of the components here with me.","rew":"Experience: 2,100\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The longer I stay here, the more tempted I am to partake in these races, ‹name›. Truly boggling...\nHave you found the elixirs yet? Once I can tell if the egg is going to be healthy or not, I'll return it to you to hold onto until it's prepared to hatch.\nLet me know.","done":"Wonderful. These will do nicely. Give me a moment to mix together my components and we shall see how well this egg is going to do.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.3,"y":74.7,"n":"Quentin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2962":{"id":2962,"t":"The Only Cure is More Green Glow","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 4,400 experience instead of 2,450, 1.8 times as much. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Travel to Gnomeregan and bring back High Potency Radioactive Fallout. Be warned, the fallout is unstable and will collapse rather quickly.\nOzzie will also require your Heavy Leaden Collection Phial when the task is complete.\nHigh Potency Radioactive Fallout\nHeavy Leaden Collection Phial\nProvided: Heavy Leaden Collection Phial","desc":"Not only was your sample insufficient in quantity, it was also impure.\nWhat we require is more green glow. The troggs are obviously not irradiated sufficiently to fulfill our needs. You will have to go into Gnomeregan and bring back some radioactive fallout, straight from the tap. I am speaking of the irradiated slimes, lurkers and horrors. Be warned, the containment of this type of fallout is difficult. You may need to make several attempts with the phial until a suitable sampling is recovered.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400","back":"Hrm, you're not glowing. That's a good sign.","done":"<Ozzie examines you.> Impressive, you still have all of your limbs. Now it's time to see what this stuff can do!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":45.9,"y":49.4,"n":"Ozzie Togglevolt","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"562":{"id":562,"t":"Stormwind Ho!","lv":32,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Daggerspine Shorehunters and 10 Daggerspine Sirens for Lieutenant Farren Orinelle in Southshore.\nDaggerspine Shorehunter slain : 0/ 10\nDaggerspine Siren slain : 0/ 10","desc":"My former mentor in the Stormwind city guard sent a message to me that Alliance High Command is becoming concerned with the threat posed by the naga. From what he's heard, there's good chances for promotion--or at least reassignment--for anyone who proves valuable in this regard.\nThere's just one small problem... I can't handle the naga, ‹name›. Oh sure, I could break up a drunken barroom brawl, or haul off a belligerent beggar, but the naga are too much for me. You've got to help me, ‹name›!","rew":"You will receive:\nFish Gutter\nExperience: 1,950","back":"I've a letter ready to go to Major Samuelson in Stormwind. All I need are the results.","done":"With the naga put down in Southshore, I'll be a shoe-in to be reassigned. I'll get to see Stormwind again... get away from this Light-forsaken port.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":51.5,"y":58.4,"n":"Lieutenant Farren Orinelle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"92482":{"id":92482,"t":"The way of the hunter","lv":2,"min":2,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Read the Scribbled Note and then speak with Tai'ree Farsight in Thendal Grove.\nProvided: Scribbled Note","desc":"While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident hunter trainer--Tai'ree Farsight--left this note for you. You can find her just over yonder near the center of the village. Read the note then seek her out.","back":"<Tai'ree nods at you curtly.>","done":"The way of the ‹class› is fraught with danger, and only those with the keenest senses and quickest reflexes can thrive in the wilds. I look at you and I am reminded of myself when I stood before my mentor, so many years ago. I believe that you have what it takes, but in the end that is up to you alone.\nSpeak with me again if you wish to take your next steps.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42,"y":23.4,"n":"Rorian the Dayseeker","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42.4,"y":23.6,"n":"Tai'ree Farsight","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"6082":{"id":6082,"t":"Taming the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame an Armored Scorpid. Practice your skills, then return to Thotar at Razor Hill.\nTaming Rod\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"The final creature you need to tame is one you should strive to emulate; the armored scorpid. It strikes quickly and confidently; to control a force such as this is your fate as a hunter.\nWhen you return, I will bestow you with the skills you will need to tame an animal of your choosing; this creature will be yours to command. Under your control, your pet will gain experience alongside you. I will also show you how to call it and dismiss it as you wish.","rew":"You will learn: Taming Lesson\nExperience: 850","back":"Were you able to tame the scorpid?","done":"You have learned all I can teach you, ‹name›. It is time for you to take what you have learned here and choose a pet of your own.\nHere you are, ‹name›. I will now give you the power to tame a beast, as well as call it and dismiss it as you see fit. Use your new skills with pride; you have earned them.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":51.8,"y":43.5,"n":"Thotar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"6722":{"id":6722,"t":"The Hunter's Path","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Dazalar in Dolanaar.","desc":"Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.\nYou must see Dazalar in Dolanaar. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Yes, it is time, ‹class›.\nStormwind City Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":67.4,"y":36.3,"n":"Einris Brightspear","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.7,"y":59.5,"n":"Dazalar","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"8882":{"id":8882,"t":"Cluster Launcher","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Coin of Ancestry","rew":"You will receive:\nSchematic: Cluster Launcher Lunar Festival Fireworks Pack","back":"The most splendid fireworks shows must include cluster rockets, and those cluster rockets must be fired from cluster launchers! Is it not then logical for you to learn the secrets of making cluster launchers? Bring me coins of ancestry and I will give this knowledge to you.","done":"Here is your schematic. Study it closely, and learn...\nGood luck, ‹name›. May your celebrations rival that of the Lunar Festival itself!","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":53.8,"y":35.3,"n":"Fariel Starsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8722":{"id":8722,"t":"Meadowrun the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":66,"y":47.8,"n":"Elder Meadowrun","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8642":{"id":8642,"t":"Silvervein the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":32.9,"y":46.3,"n":"Elder Silvervein","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9362":{"id":9362,"t":"Warlord Krellian","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,500, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Retrieve the Prismatic Shell for Archmage Xylem. The Archmage resides in a tower atop the cliffs of Azshara.\nPrismatic Shell Warlord Krellian","desc":"There isn't much time, ‹name›! My scrying spells have revealed a powerful source of magic. I cannot leave the tower, and would ask you to kill the vile creature in possession of this artifact.\nThe pathetic little cretin is known as Warlord Krellian, hiding behind his guards in the Temple of Zin-Malor. Burn him to ashes and take the prismatic shell he covets so dearly.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"There is not time to waste! Have you the shell?","done":"I must say, this shell has a strange aura. It seems only fitting that part of your reward for retrieving it would be to test its magical capabilities...","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":29.2,"y":40.2,"n":"Archmage Xylem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"6642":{"id":6642,"t":"Favor Amongst the Brotherhood, Dark Iron Ore","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Dark Iron Ore Dark Iron Deposit , Warbringer Construct 13.4 % , Wrath Hammer Construct 13 % , Ragereaver Golem 13 % and 4 more","back":"Dark Iron, while plentiful in the Depths, is still a valued commodity amongst the Brotherhood. The sacred arms and armaments of Ragnaros favor Dark Iron.\nFor every 10 pieces of Dark Iron Ore you offer, favor amongst the Brotherhood you will gain.","done":"Your offering has been accepted. Favor you have gained. Continue and you shall be allowed access to the ancient trades.\nStart Lokhtos Darkbargainer End Lokhtos Darkbargainer Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6642","cats":["molten-core"]},"9042":{"id":9042,"t":"Dreadnaught Bracers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Korfax at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Dreadnaught Bracers if you bring him the following items: 1 Desecrated Bracers, 6 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 1 Nexus Crystal.\nDesecrated Bracers Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Grand Widow Faerlina 0 % in Naxxramas , Anub'Rekhan 0 % in Naxxramas\n6 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\nNexus Crystal","desc":"During your battles with the Scourge in Naxxramas, should you come across desecrated battlements and wartorn plate scraps, return them to me and I shall craft for you a piece of armor worn by heroes.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreadnaught Bracers\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Dreadnaught Bracers.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":72,"y":48.5,"n":"Korfax, Champion of the Light","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"91282":{"id":91282,"t":"A second home","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the fortress of Bandarion Keep and report to Breton Samuels there.","desc":"It is encouraging to see my newly risen brothers and sisters thrive as you have. It is only through community and shared faith that we can truly realize our full potential however, and to that end we've begun to form a new paladin order right here in Tirisfal.\nIf you wish to learn more, you should visit our monastery at Northface Rock. It is called Bandarion Keep. It's on the bluffs just northwest of the Solliden Farmstead, and should be hard to miss.","rew":"Money: 1 0 gold, 1 silver, 0 copper Experience: 220","done":"Another fresh recruit? Welcome to Tyr's Watch, brother.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":60.2,"y":52.6,"n":"Shari Stilwell","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":21.8,"y":45.2,"n":"Breton Samuels","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"1442":{"id":1442,"t":"Seeking the Kor Gem","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 875 experience instead of 440, 1.99 times as much. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Bring a Kor Gem to Thundris Windweaver in Darkshore.\nCorrupted Kor Gem Blackfathom Sea Witch 50 % , Blackfathom Oracle 50 % , Blackfathom Tide Priestess 50 %","desc":"Greetings, ‹name›. What can I do for one who follows a holy path?\nAh, yes, Stilwell, the blacksmith... from long ago. I remember him well, though, I have not heard his name in some time.\nHe never struck me as an impudent man, so I can only assume his desire for a Kor gem is noble.\nIf you truly wish for one of the gems, then you must head to the northwest of Ashenvale. You will find Blackfathom Deeps there within some ancient ruins. The naga who still use the gems are down below. Do not go alone, ‹class›.","rew":"You will receive:\nPurified Kor Gem\nExperience: 875","back":"I would be less trustful of one not on a holy path if they came asking about a Kor gem. But I trust your kind more than some of my kin. I do not judge your entire order based on the actions of just one of your fallen kind.","done":"This is indeed the gem Stilwell desires, but before I can allow you to bring it to him, it must be purified of corruption--the naga wenches imbue the gems with power, that much is true, but of their own, evil kind.\nLet Stilwell know that its power is intact, and it should work well for whatever ritual he wishes it to be part of.\nI hope you know what you're doing, ‹class›, this is no simple item you possess.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":40.1,"n":"Thundris Windweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"95042":{"id":95042,"t":"Seeking the kor gem","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring a Kor Gem to Ulric Frostveil in Ashenvale.\nCorrupted Kor Gem","desc":"A Forsaken paladin... here in Ashenvale? Amusing.\nSo you seek a Kor Gem? Unsurprising as these are sometimes employed to empower magical weapons and implements by the paladins of the alliance. Why should a fallen paladin like you be any different?\nIf you truly desire one of the gems, then you must head north to the ruins known as Blackfathom Deeps. The naga who still use the gems are down below. Do not go alone, ‹class›.","rew":"You will receive:\nPurified Kor Gem\nExperience: 2,000\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"Kor gems can be used for great acts of evil. Far be it from me to judge if your intentions are pure. It matters not to me.","done":"You'll no doubt notice the corruption that permeates this gem. For your purposes, The magic needed to dispel the evil that the naga witches have infused into the gem is rather simple. A shame really, there's much one could learn from such powers.\nI don't suppose you'd be willing to abandon whatever quest caused you seek this gem, and sell it to me instead? It could prove valuable to my... academic pursuits.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":11.8,"y":34.4,"n":"Ulric Frostveil","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"2242":{"id":2242,"t":"Destiny Calls","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Sethir the Ancient and bring back any clues that you may discover to Syurna.\nSethir's Journal","desc":"We believe there is one being that may be able to help us understand what is happening to the forests of Teldrassil. Unfortunately, getting the creature to cooperate has proven disastrous.\nHe hides on a branch at the outskirts of the Oracle Glade. All who have so far approached the satyr, whether through force or diplomacy, have met with doom. Perhaps stealth is the answer, ‹name›.\nFind what Sethir the Ancient carries in his packs and report back to me.","rew":"You will receive:\nBlade of Cunning\nExperience: 850","back":"Have you anything to report from Sethir the Ancient, ‹name›?","done":"This is grim news, ‹name›. It would seem that the sickness which has gripped the forests and rivers of Darkshore has begun to taint our home.\nYou have served us well, but there is nothing more you can do here. Take this blade as a reward for your service to Teldrassil.\nDarnassus Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":37,"y":21.9,"n":"Syurna","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"3442":{"id":3442,"t":"The Flawless Flame","lv":48,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 4 Hearts of Flame and 4 globes of Golem Oil and return the items to Kalaran Windblade.\n4 Heart of Flame Inferno Elemental 31 % , Blazing Elemental 29 % , Magma Elemental 26 %\n4 Golem Oil Magma Elemental 30 % , Tempered War Golem 28 % , Heavy War Golem 27 %","desc":"You have made the right decision, ‹name›.\nWe must strike where we will do the most damage: the four sentry towers.\nWith the four towers in flames, we can initiate an offensive before they have time to react.\nYou will need the proper tool to set the towers ablaze. To make the tool requires some materials.\nBring me four hearts of flame and four golem oil and I shall craft the torch of flawless flame.\nThe golems and elementals in these lands should be your first target.","rew":"Money: 1 40 1 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400","back":"Have you collected the materials?","done":"Well done, ‹name›. We are almost ready.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":39.1,"y":39,"n":"Kalaran Windblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8242":{"id":8242,"t":"Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Heavy Leather","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Incendosaur Scale Incendosaur\n10 Heavy Leather Advanced Target Dummy 90 % , Felsteel Chest 3.6 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 2.5 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 2.5 % and 4 more\nCoal Dalaran Miner , Blazing Elemental 28.4 % , Inferno Elemental 24.7 % , Molten Giant 24.7 % and 4 more","desc":"Let's not waste more of my precious time with jibber jabber, ‹race›. It's time to focus on replenishing our dwindling fiery flux supply.\nWhat I'm gonna need from you is the following:\n*Incendosaur scales.\n*Heavy Leather.\n*Coal.\nI'll take all that you can offer!\nAnd you'll do it fast if you wanna get in good with the Brotherhood.","back":"Let's not waste more of my precious time with jibber jabber, ‹race›. It's time to focus on replenishing our dwindling fiery flux supply.\nWhat I'm gonna need from you is the following:\n*Incendosaur scales.\n*Heavy Leather.\n*Coal.\nI'll take all that you can offer!\nAnd you'll do it fast if you wanna get in good with the Brotherhood.","done":"There's always room for more fiery flux, junior. Keep it comin'... unless I tell you to stop.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":38.8,"y":28.5,"n":"Master Smith Burninate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8322":{"id":8322,"t":"Rotten Eggs","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Place the Rotten Eggs in the main brew keg located inside the Southshore Inn.\nRotten Eggs\nProvided: Rotten Eggs","desc":"The humans of Southshore love their ale, and as such they prize the ale served at the Southshore Inn. With the chaos of Hallow's End now upon them, we can use it to ruin their latest batch of beverages for weeks - if not months to come!\nTake these rotten eggs and place them in the main brew keg inside the Southshore Inn. Your presence alone will cause strife, so be prepared to defend yourself!\nOnce you've given Southshore a taste they'll not soon forget, return to me here at the festival!","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+25 reputation with Horde","done":"The keg is filled with ale.\nHaving successfully fought your way inside the inn, you now place the eggs inside the keg. You can smell the foul odor permeating the air...\nTirisfal Glades Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":55.6,"y":69.9,"n":"Darkcaller Yanka","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":51.4,"y":59,"n":"Keg","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"7042":{"id":7042,"t":"Stolen Winter Veil Treats","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Locate the Smokywood Pastures investigator that has gone missing in the snowy regions of the Alterac Mountains.","desc":"Listen... not to shatter the magic of the season here, but Smokywood Pastures could use some assistance - the kind you adventuring types are known to give.\nWe're missing an important shipment of treats that was restocking us for the season, and now we're missing the agent of Smokywood Pastures that we sent out to the field to find it! Please - the shipment was last reported in the Alterac Mountains, and that's where our man went to look for it.\nSee if both are out there, safe and sound!","rew":"Experience: 1,650","done":"Y-y-you can h-h-hear me! Thank the b-b-bottom line!\nI'm not really a s-s-snowman - my n-n-name is Sacks, and I w-w-work for the Ironforge b-b-branch of Smokywood Pastures... I g-g-got sent out here to look for a m-m-missing package, when I was attacked by a c-c-creature I have never seen b-b-before!\nSo v-v-very cold...\nDun Morogh Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.5,"y":31.9,"n":"Wulmort Jinglepocket","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":29.9,"y":61,"n":"The Abominable Greench","e":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":35.4,"y":72.5,"n":"Strange Snowman","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"6962":{"id":6962,"t":"Treats for Great-father Winter","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Gingerbread Cookies and an Ice Cold Milk to Great-father Winter in Orgrimmar.\n5 Gingerbread Cookie\nIce Cold Milk Barrel of Milk , Foreman Silixiz 60 % , Wenikee Boltbucket 58.3 % , Takar the Seer 40 % and 4 more","desc":"Hey, can you do Great-father Winter a favor, um, little boy/girl?\nNot to needlessly talk about myself in the third person, but Great-father Winter has been at this all day and he could use a treat himself. Some gingerbread cookies and ice cold milk to wash them down with would really hit the spot. Think you could be a friend to the Great-father and fetch some for me?","rew":"You will receive:\nSmokywood Pastures Gift Pack\nExperience: 1,650\n+25 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"All this talk of treats has given me a hankering for some myself. Mmmm... gingerbread cookies and milk...","done":"You're quite the helper to ol' Great-father Winter there, ‹name›. Have a great Feast of Winter Veil.\nHere's a little something... you know, for the effort.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.5,"y":69.2,"n":"Great-father Winter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"1522":{"id":1522,"t":"Call of Fire","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Kranal Fiss in the Barrens.","desc":"Fire be witcha, mon. I see you be strong in da ways of earth already, an' me tinkin' you be ready to talk to Kranal.\nKranal live north of da Crossroads in da Barrens. He be strong in da ways of da elements and can teach ya da ways of fire... if you tink you be ready.\nHe be easy ta find, just don' go too far--ya go too far an' ya find yerself in da elves' lands.","rew":"Experience: 420","done":"Hmmm, Searn sent you to me, did he?\nWell then, Searn could always be trusted, so that must mean you're ready to take part of the next sapta--the sapta of fire.\nI see it in your eyes already, the burning, the desire. You've tasted power, and now you're ready for more of it. Patience, ‹name›. Remember what earth taught you. Power and destruction will come easily, but you must still know when to stay your hand.\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38,"y":37.7,"n":"Searn Firewarder","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":56,"y":19.9,"n":"Kranal Fiss","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"93122":{"id":93122,"t":"Checking things out","lv":43,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and investigate centaur points of interest within Shen'dralas. Then return to Nerlokh at the entrance of Valley of Bones with your findings.","desc":"We have all underestimated the power and presence of the Magram clan in this area, but this could prove an advantage.\nWith so many of their own distracted and their refusal to accept other clans' exiles, who is left to defend the village? What of their Khan?\nI need you to go into the valley, deeper than you have gone before, and look around. If the Magram are as well fortified here as they seem, they may have left themselves vulnerable at their village...\nLevel 43 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 39 41 46 54 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 93122\nThe chain\n4 quests from level 42 to 43, 9,810 XP in all.\n1 [ 42 ] Saving Our Own\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis clan, and rescue 5 Gelkis Captives within the Valley of Bones.\n2,550 XP\n[ 42 ] Bone Burying\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan, and dispel the curses from 8 failed summons throughout the Valley of Bones.\n3,450 XP\n2 [ 43 ] Checking Things Out this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and investigate centaur points of interest within Shen'dralas.\n360 XP\n3 [ 42 ] Khan Jehn\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and slay Khan Jhen at Magram Village.\n3,450 XP","cats":["shendralas"]},"6322":{"id":6322,"t":"Michael Garrett","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Gordon's Crate to Michael Garrett.\nGordon's Crate\nProvided: Gordon's Crate","desc":"I have placed the Sepulcher's supplies into this crate. If you have already visited the Sepulcher and spoken with their bat master, then you may ride a bat back to him.\nSpeak with the Undercity's bat master, Michael Garrett. He can provide you with a bat to the Sepulcher.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Undercity","back":"If you must travel a long distance, then a bat is your best option.","done":"This crate must reach the Sepulcher in Silverpine? That is easily done; our bats fly there daily.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":61.5,"y":41.8,"n":"Gordon Wendham","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":63.3,"y":48.6,"n":"Michael Garrett","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"482":{"id":482,"t":"Dalaran's Intentions","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher.","desc":"Of course! How could I have forgotten?\nAmbermill was one of the sites earmarked by the Kirin Tor, noted because it houses a dormant ley energy node. The wizards must be planning to reactivate the node and use its energies for some greater purpose.\nWe cannot allow this to happen...\nIt will take a great amount of power to activate the area's ley energies, we can stall them by taking the pendants away from the wizards.\nRelay this information to Allister, he will decide a course of action.","rew":"Experience: 100\n+10 reputation with Undercity","done":"Ill news you bring, ‹name›. If Dalar is correct--and I've no reason to believe he isn't--we must move quickly.\nI must confer with him on our plan of attack. But in the meanwhile we will have to delay their progress.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44.2,"y":39.8,"n":"Dalar Dawnweaver","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44,"y":40.9,"n":"Shadow Priest Allister","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"84402":{"id":84402,"t":"Necromancy 101","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Necromancy 101","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nNecromancy 101 (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.6,"y":79.4,"n":"Jennea Cannon","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.4,"y":32.4,"n":"Oran Snakewrithe","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"6402":{"id":6402,"t":"Stormwind Rendezvous","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Stormwind City and venture to the city gates. Speak with Squire Rowe so that he may let Marshal Windsor know that you have arrived.","desc":"You are to meet with Windsor at the gates of Stormwind.\nWhat Windsor is about to unveil will shake the very foundation of the kingdom!\nDo not attempt to venture there alone, ‹name›. You must amass an army! Gather your compatriots. To arms!","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"Before we begin, I ask that you first gather an army. We face a dragon, after all!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.7,"y":69,"n":"Marshal Maxwell","s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"5122":{"id":5122,"t":"The Medallion of Faith","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Medallion of Faith Malor's Strongbox in Stratholme","back":"The power of this chapel gives me the strength to resist the corruption in my heart. If I leave it, I will become a death knight. But there is a medallion, the medallion of faith, that will give me the strength I need to leave.\nPlease, ‹name›, retrieve the medallion. It is guarded by Malor the Zealous, a crazed member of the Scarlet Brotherhood who resides deep in the Scarlet Bastion in western Stratholme.","done":"You retrieved the medallion! Now I will be able to leave the chapel and perform my duty.\nThat duty is to kill the beast who helped corrupt me and so many of my brothers and sisters, Baron Rivendare!\nStart Aurius Stratholme End Aurius Stratholme Level 60 , requires level 55 Difficulty 55 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 5122\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 9,950 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] The Medallion of Faith this quest\nAurius Stratholme\n2 [ 60 ] Aurius' Reckoning\nAurius Stratholme\n9,950 XP","cats":["stratholme"]},"5282":{"id":5282,"t":"The Restless Souls","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 8,850, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Use Egan's Blaster on the ghostly and spectral citizens of Stratholme. When the restless souls break free from their ghostly shells, use the blaster again - freedom will be theirs!\nFree 15 Restless Souls and return to Egan.\nSouls Freed : 0/ 15\nProvided: Egan's Blaster","desc":"I draw my power - my will to continue living and breathing - from the unmitigated hatred I have for the Scourge and all that they have done. I am, however, no zealot. There are those, like the Scarlet Crusade, who would sooner destroy the innocent undead than lend them even an ounce of compassion.\nWhich brings me to this: My blaster. It will unchain the tortured souls from Stratholme.\nUse it on the ghosts that haunt the ransacked streets. Free their souls.","rew":"You will receive:\nTestament of Hope\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300","back":"Compassion is what separates us from the animals, ‹name›. Remember that...","done":"<Egan wipes a tear from his eye.>\nDid you see my mother, ‹name›? Did you free her?\nYou are a shining example of decency. For your troubles...","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":11.4,"y":26.6,"n":"Egan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stratholme"]},"82":{"id":82,"t":"Noxious Lair Investigation","lv":47,"min":39,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring five Centipaar insect parts from the Noxious Lair to Alchemist Pestlezugg in Gadgetzan.\n5 Centipaar Insect Parts Centipaar Worker 50 % , Centipaar Tunneler 50 % , Centipaar Sandreaver 50 % , Centipaar Wasp 20 % and 2 more","desc":"All right now, these reports about the bugs... what we know is that they are draining the water pools that used to be where the Noxious Lair is. What we DON'T know is, well, everything else.\nLet's figure out who our enemy is first! I want you to head into the Noxious Lair and get some parts off of those critters. Get five from the Centipaar there and bring them to Alchemist Pestlezugg for him to dink with. With him on the case, we'll figure out what they are!","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,150\n+75 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"You're Junior Surveyor ‹name›, yes? Quickly now, there is a dire situation at hand! Do you have the insect parts that Fizzledowser said you would?!","done":"Good work - I'll start my analysis on these now! I can tell you right from the start though... these are nothing like any insect form I have ever seen. It's almost as if these bugs are being controlled by an outside force or something.\nYou need to go talk to Fizzledowser right away; apparently there is an emergency that he needs your help with on the double! I'm not sure, but I think it involves more of the bugs in the Tanaris desert!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.2,"y":27.5,"n":"Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.9,"y":27,"n":"Alchemist Pestlezugg","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"162":{"id":162,"t":"Rise of the Silithid","lv":49,"min":39,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Insect Analysis Report to Gracina Spiritmight in Darnassus.\nInsect Analysis Report\nProvided: Insect Analysis Report","desc":"I urge you to take this report to someone who has working knowledge in this kind of thing.\nI know this night elf scholar named Gracina Spiritmight. She's spent a lot of time studying life forms that are unique to the ecology of Azeroth; she's a historian to boot! If you want someone to help figure out what exactly this threat is, and more importantly how to stop it, give her the report. We'll need the help.\nLast I heard, she was residing in the Temple of the Moon, located in Darnassus.","rew":"Experience: 5,700\n+150 reputation with Gadgetzan\n+150 reputation with Alliance","back":"Peace and tranquility be upon you, stranger. Why have you sought me out this day?","done":"This report... we night elves know of the terror mentioned here. Fizzledowser was wise to send this, and you, to me.\nThese creatures will consume the Tanaris desert rapidly; they are nothing short of one of the greatest menaces we all will ever face. Familiarize yourself with this name, ‹name›: silithid. The insects mentioned here are the silithid, and they are the tools of one of the greatest threats that both the Horde and Alliance face.\nIf only we were smart enough to see that before.\nTanaris Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.2,"y":27.5,"n":"Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":41.8,"y":85.6,"n":"Gracina Spiritmight","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"3362":{"id":3362,"t":"Thistleshrub Valley","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Tran'rek in Gadgetzan wants you to kill 8 Gnarled Thistleshrubs and 8 Thistleshrub Rootshapers.\nGnarled Thistleshrub slain : 0/ 8\nThistleshrub Rootshaper slain : 0/ 8","desc":"Have you ever seen Thistleshrub Valley? It's a mighty dangerous place, ‹name›.\nThose strange beasts there, I don't trust them for a minute! Gnarled thistleshrubs and thistleshrub rootshapers, that's what I think they were called...\nAnyhow, I want to get into the valley, but with so many of those thistleshrubs around, there's no way I'm going back there. But here's where you come in -- if you clear some of them out, I just might think about going back. What do you think, ‹name›? Help me out?","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"I'd like to take a closer look at that cactus in the valley... So leave some of it in one piece, will ya?","done":"They're that big? I might have to rethink my plan...\nBut you did hold up your end of the bargain, so here's what I promised.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.6,"y":26.8,"n":"Tran'rek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"5842":{"id":5842,"t":"Welcome!","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Shadowglen Gift Voucher to Orenthil Whisperwind.\nShadowglen Gift Voucher\nProvided: Shadowglen Gift Voucher","desc":"Welcome to the World of Warcraft!\nAs special thanks for purchasing the World of Warcraft Collector's Edition, turn in this gift voucher to Orenthil Whisperwind in Shadowglen. You'll then be given a gift: a little companion to join you on your quest for adventure and glory.\nThanks again, and enjoy your stay in the World of Warcraft!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDiablo Stone Panda Collar Zergling Leash","back":"Greetings! It is a pleasure to meet you!\nI see you have a special voucher. Give it to me and I will offer you something in exchange.","done":"You are indeed a special hero, ‹name›. We welcome you to the world of Azeroth, and offer you one of these unique gifts!","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":58.8,"y":44.4,"n":"Orenthil Whisperwind","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"3522":{"id":3522,"t":"Iverron's Antidote","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Iverron's Antidote to Iverron before the time limit is up. Iverron can be found by the cave to the north.\nIverron's Antidote\nProvided: Iverron's Antidote","desc":"The antidote is ready, ‹name›. Please see that Iverron drinks it.\nThere is something that you should know -- the antidote -- it will only remain viable for 5 minutes. You must get it to him in time.\nSpeed be with you, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSedgeweed Britches Barkmail Vest\nExperience: 450\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Oh... ‹name›, I'm so glad you have returned.","done":"What is this, ‹name›?\nOh, I knew Dirania would be able to help me!\n<Iverron drinks the antidote>\nI'm always getting into trouble and Dirania, well, she always manages to help me out of it.\nI am feeling much better, but I think I will sit here for a while longer, until I feel completely better. Well, that, and I was hoping you'd clear a path for me through those vicious Webwood spiders...","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.9,"y":42,"n":"Dirania Silvershine","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":54.6,"y":33,"n":"Iverron","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"3922":{"id":3922,"t":"Nugget Slugs","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 15 Nugget Slugs to Wenikee Boltbucket in the Barrens.\n15 Nugget Slug Tool Bucket","desc":"I want to fix this samophlange, but to do that I'm going to need some supplies. I ran out of seventeen-point-five gauge nugget slugs and I'm going to need a bunch of those for the work ahead.\nThe closest place to get them is the Sludge Fen to the east. The Venture Company usually keeps them in their tool buckets. Go to the Sludge Fen and look in the tool buckets you find there, then return to me when you've gathered enough nugget slugs.","rew":"Experience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Ratchet\n+50 reputation with Horde","back":"Do you have the nugget slugs, ‹name›? I've been eyeing this Samophlange and I can't wait to tinker with it.","done":"Great, you got them! Now I can get to work...","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":49.1,"y":11.2,"n":"Wenikee Boltbucket","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"882":{"id":882,"t":"Ishamuhale","lv":19,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ishamuhale's Fang to Jorn at Camp Taurajo.\nIshamuhale's Fang Ishamuhale","desc":"Ishamuhale, Speartooth, is the fiercest sunscale raptor of the Barrens. He does not hunt for sport, nor for food. He hunts because hunting is his passion. He kills because it is his nature to kill.\nAnd you will learn of his nature, ‹name›, for your path now follows the taloned tracks of Ishamuhale.\nBegin the hunt. Slay his favorite prey, a zhevra, then bring its carcass to the dead tree northwest of Ratchet. Ishamuhale will smell the carcass and be drawn to it.\nBe ready when he comes.","rew":"Experience: 1,800\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"‹name›, have you bested Ishamuhale?","done":"This fang is merely a token, but what it represents is profound.\nIshamuhale's strength is in you, ‹name›. May you use it with temperance. That is your burden.\nThat is your honor.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.9,"y":59.1,"n":"Jorn Skyseer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"5042":{"id":5042,"t":"Agamaggan's Strength","lv":20,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Blood Shard Bristleback Geomancer 49 % , Bristleback Thornweaver 48.8 % , Bristleback Water Seeker 48.7 % , Bristleback Hunter 34 % and 4 more","rew":"You will learn: Agamaggan's Strength","back":"I will need 4 blood shards if you wish Agamaggan's strength, ‹race›.\nYour foes will cower before your strength were you to be given this blessing. <snort>\nThe Razormane's greatest warriors are infused with such power!","done":"If only Mangletooth were free to see you decimate those who betrayed him! <snort>\nI thank you for destroying more of the Bristleback by gathering these shards. Please, continue to do so, and I will continue to aid you. <snort>","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.5,"y":59.3,"n":"Mangletooth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"7842":{"id":7842,"t":"Another Message to the Wildhammer","lv":48,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Otho Moji'ko at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to bring him 10 Long Elegant Feathers from the gryphons that inhabit the Hinterlands. Return to him once this task is complete.\nGryphons are known to inhabit every region of the Hinterlands.\n10 Long Elegant Feather Granistad 46 % , Wild Gryphon 42.9 % , Trained Razorbeak 40.2 % , Razorbeak Skylord 38.8 % and 4 more","desc":"They say the Wildhammer and gryphon are as close to each other as troll and mate. Disgusting, but we be able to use this to our advantage, mon. We send them another message.\nKill all the gryphons you see in the Hinterlands, collect their feathers. From this we make the final message.","rew":"Experience: 5,450\n+150 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"The last message gonna scare them off for sure. Either that or make them very, very angry.","done":"Oh, mon, this gonna be good. One more step to go and Wildhammer see that they can't mess with troll!","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":79.4,"y":79.1,"n":"Otho Moji'ko","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"5762":{"id":5762,"t":"Hemet Nesingwary","lv":31,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Kravel's Crate to Hemet Nesingwary in Stranglethorn.\nKravel's Crate\nProvided: Kravel's Crate","desc":"I have a package for an old customer of mine, a dwarf named Hemet Nesingwary. The package took weeks to arrive, and Hemet's long gone by now. He said he was going to Stranglethorn to hunt the beasts there, but he left me some money to send his delivery when I could.\nHemet's a rich dwarf and it's a good idea to keep up relations with the rich ones, yeah? So... you want to deliver the package for me?\nI heard Hemet has a camp in Stranglethorn, north of Grom'gol.","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,250","back":"Is that desert dust on your collar?\nHm... if my nose tells true, I'd say it's not desert dust, it's desert salt! Been to the Shimmering Flats, have you?","done":"Great, my package from Koalbeard! Thank you ‹name›. This crate holds special-gauge ammunition, and it'll serve us well out in the jungle!\nHere's your pay, and tell me, how is crusty old Kravel these days? Still up to no good I'd wager...\nThousand Needles Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.8,"y":77.3,"n":"Kravel Koalbeard","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.7,"y":10.8,"n":"Hemet Nesingwary","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1122":{"id":1122,"t":"Report Back to Fizzlebub","lv":44,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Fool's Stout report to Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay.\nFool's Stout Report\nProvided: Fool's Stout Report","desc":"That Fool's Stout worked great! I placed a bet on the next race, and... let's hope the crew you got drunk did a number on their car!\nThere's only one more task for you -- take this note back to Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay. He'll want to know of the successful test.\nAnd hopefully we can get more of that Fool's Stout for future races!","rew":"Experience: 1,850","back":"Hello ‹name›. How'd that stout work out? It's strong stuff, isn't it?","done":"It says here that the fool's stout was a success. That's good news!\nIf you ever want more of the stuff, then let me know and I'll have you gather more of Zanzil's Mixture.\nThousand Needles Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.8,"y":77.3,"n":"Kravel Koalbeard","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.1,"y":77.2,"n":"Crank Fizzlebub","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"3762":{"id":3762,"t":"Assisting Arch Druid Runetotem","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.","desc":"Excuse me ‹class›, but I'd like just a moment of your time if possible.\nThe Cenarion Circle in Thunder Bluff is most interested in seasoned adventurers such as yourself to lend them aid in a vital research project. While I do not know the specifics, I can inform you that none other than Hamuul Runetotem is spearheading this research.\nPlease - if you are interested, speak with him directly on the Elder Rise within Thunder Bluff proper.","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Greetings, ‹class›; I am glad you are interested in assisting our research. There is much to do, and I would be doing you a disservice if I informed you that the work this entails is not dangerous. Hopefully this will not scare you off... but from the looks of you, I take it that danger is something that you have dealt with before.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":45.8,"y":64.7,"n":"Innkeeper Pala","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":78.6,"y":28.6,"n":"Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"2882":{"id":2882,"t":"Cuergo's Gold","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Cuergo's gold!\nCuergo's Key Treasure Hunting Buccaneer , Treasure Hunting Swashbuckler , Treasure Hunting Pirate","desc":"This map shows a stretch of beach with a southern face. Below the map are words, elegantly written...\nSouth of Wheedle\nSouth of home\nFind a mast and flag and bones\nDig you there, if you be bold\nDig and claim Cuergo's gold!\nA key you'll need and a key you'll see\nThe men you face take blood as fee.","rew":"You will receive:\nCuergo's Hidden Treasure","back":"This chest is locked!","done":"Captain Cuergo's hidden treasure awaits!\nTanaris Open the zone on the world map Start an item: Cuergo's Treasure Map End Pirate's Treasure! Level 45 , requires level 40 Difficulty 40 41 43 48 57 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 2882","cats":["treasure-map"]},"722":{"id":722,"t":"Amulet of Secrets","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Hammertoe's Amulet and return it to him in Uldaman.\nHammertoe's Amulet Magregan Deepshadow","desc":"Ye're brave... <cough>... to come into Uldaman fer me, ‹class›.\nIf ye're really here to help... ol' Hammertoe, then... <cough>... you'll need to find... me amulet.\nDeepshadow's got it... Magregan Deepshadow. He's 'round here... in the ruins fer sure. That amulet'll lead 'em... <cough>... right to the scrolls if he ain't stopped. It's up to you, ‹name›. Please... get that amulet.\nThe scrolls will surely help the Dark Irons create even more powerful golems. I just know it. I can feel it in me bones.","rew":"Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"The Shadowforge clan... <cough> is dangerous. Be careful. <cough> You must find the amulet.","done":"Ha! <cough cough>\nAh knew you'd find me amulet, ‹name›.\n<weeze> Well done indeed, ‹name›. <cough>","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":37.3,"y":85.8,"n":"Hammertoe Grez","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"4642":{"id":4642,"t":"Melding of Influences","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Merged Ooze Sample to Chemist Fuely in Undercity.\nMerged Ooze Sample Gargantuan Ooze\nProvided: Encased Corrupt Ooze","desc":"Here is some encased ooze created from the Felwood samples you recovered. Take the case to Un'Goro Crater and find a pure ooze... the primal variety will do nicely. When you get close enough, release the ooze in the case, and let us see what the two think of one another.\nAfter the experiment concludes, bring me a sample of whatever is left over. I will await you here in the Apothecarium.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nChemist's Ring Chemist's Smock\nExperience: 7,050\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"How goes the experiment, ‹name›? I will continue to study the samples you've recovered for me--I am starting to see why Lady Sylvanas is so interested in these creatures. If they are truly part of the Old Gods, then who knows how it can be used to our benefit.","done":"Oh, most excellent, ‹name›. This is most excellent.\nSuch a tale. Who would have thought the two would interact with one another in such a way... I will have to spend more time looking at the environmental issues that cause changes in these creatures.\nI will continue my research for now. Perhaps we will speak again soon. Until then, I wish you well.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":47.5,"y":73.3,"n":"Chemist Fuely","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"962":{"id":962,"t":"Serpentbloom","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 20s instead of 10s. Gives 3,300 experience instead of 1,350, 2.44 times as much. New rewards: Heat Resistant Mitts, Safety Boots. Partly read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff wants you to collect 10 Serpentbloom.\n10 Serpentbloom Serpentbloom","desc":"The Royal Apothecary Society, based in the great Undercity of Lordaeron, has sent me here for a very specific service, ‹name›. Perhaps you wish to aid me, and in turn The Dark Lady in our efforts to advance the Forsaken.\nRecently I studied a rare specimen of flora named Serpentbloom. I believe in greater quantities this herb has great potential.\nUnfortunately Serpentbloom can only be found in the darkest recesses of the Wailing Caverns, a dangerous cave system located in the Barrens.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nApothecary Gloves Heat Resistant Mitts Safety Boots\nNew in Forever: Heat Resistant Mitts, Safety Boots.\nMoney: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"I am eager to see if you can gather enough Serpentbloom from the Wailing Caverns. I've sent many to do my bidding but none have returned.","done":"Ah, splendid specimens. You have done well, ‹name›.\nThunder Bluff The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":22.8,"y":20.9,"n":"Apothecary Zamah","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wailing-caverns"]},"65602":{"id":65602,"t":"What is love","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Retrieve the Wooden Figurine and bring it to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.\nWooden Figurine","desc":"You will need a powerful reagent to tempt an incubus -- an object that represents great devotion and love.\nWith my scrying, I have located a small figurine that should be suitable for your ritual.\nThousands of years ago, the figurine belonged to a young couple. The original owners are no more, but their keepsake has survived to the present day.\nFollow the road north into Ashenvale, then west and past Maestra's Post. You will see a house nestled amongst the trees. There you will find what you seek.","back":"You've returned. Successfully, I assume?","done":"<Gakin turns the wooden figurine over in his hand.>\nI sense the emotional energy residing within this artifact, undiminished by the passing of time. The incubus will be drawn to it like a fly to honey.\nTakar never disappoints.\nThe Barrens Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":49.2,"y":57,"n":"Takar the Seer","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":25.4,"y":78.4,"n":"Gakin the Darkbinder","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4962":{"id":4962,"t":"Shard of a Felhound","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Felhas Ruby and use it on one of the Felhounds found in Desolace. After successful, bring the Felhas Ruby and the Imprisoned Felhound Spirit back to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.\nFelhas Ruby\nImprisoned Felhound Spirit\nProvided: Felhas Ruby","desc":"So, you have chosen to capture the soul of a felhound, good.\nTake this ruby--with it, you will be able to capture the creature's soul. It works very similar to spells you already know: when the creature is close to dying, use the gem and it should do the rest of the work for you.\nI would suggest going to Desolace and trying your hand at any of the felhounds there. Those should do nicely.\nAfter you're successful, take both the captured spirit and your ruby to Menara.","rew":"Experience: 2,350","back":"Yes, ‹name›? Have you chosen? Infernal or felhound?\nEach choice is personal and should reflect your strengths and weaknesses. It is not unheard of for a warlock to enhance themselves further instead of making up in areas they lack. Sometimes overpowering an enemy is just as strong a tactic than becoming a more balanced spell caster.","done":"Ah, the spirit of a felhound. Well done, ‹name›.\nWhen I have both the spirit and the cleansed orb, I will merge the two for you, but not until then.\nThe Barrens Desolace","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.3,"n":"Acolyte Wytula","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"7602":{"id":7602,"t":"Flawless Fel Essence","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Impsy in Felwood has asked that you bring him three Flawless Fel Essences originating from three distinct locations.\nThe Legashi Satyrs of Azshara hold the Flawless Fel Essence of their region. The Jaedenar Legionnaires of Jaedenar hold the Flawless Fel Essence of their region. The Felguard Sentries of the Blasted Lands hold the Flawless Fel Essence of their region.\nRecover the Flawless Fel Essences and return to Impsy in Felwood.\nFlawless Fel Essence (Azshara) Legashi Hellcaller 75 % , Legashi Satyr 75 % , Legashi Rogue 75 %\nFlawless Fel Essence (Jaedenar) Jaedenar Legionnaire 75 %\nFlawless Fel Essence (Dark Portal) Felguard Sentry 75 %","desc":"If you're going to reanimate Kroshius, you're going to need Fel fire. I can make Fel fire but it's going to require some components.\nYou need to bring me flawless Fel essences from three distinct regions of the world.\nThe Legashi Satyrs of Azshara will have the first essence type; the Jaedenar legionnaires of Jaedenar the second type and the felguard sentries of the Blasted Lands the third.\nBring me back one of each essence type and I will create the Fel fire, allowing you to reanimate Kroshius.","rew":"Experience: 5,650","back":"Don't tell anyone this but Niby is daft.","done":"Give me a minute and I'll combine the essences into Fel fire.\nFelwood Azshara Blasted Lands","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":41.5,"y":45,"n":"Impsy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1682":{"id":1682,"t":"Grey Iron Weapons","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nUmbral Axe Umbral Mace Umbral Dagger Umbral Sword\nExperience: 625","done":"Here are some weapons, hot off the anvil and made with the new umbral ore you brought me!\nPlease, ‹name›, take your pick!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.9,"y":27.9,"n":"Tormus Deepforge","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1842":{"id":1842,"t":"Satyr Hooves","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 7 Uncloven Satyr Hooves to Ula'elek at Sen'jin Village in Durotar.\n7 Uncloven Satyr Hoof Bleakheart Hellcaller 80 % , Bleakheart Shadowstalker 80 % , Bleakheart Trickster 80 % , Bleakheart Satyr 80 % and 4 more","desc":"I can make you a pair of brutal gauntlets, and great magic will they hold. But first, you must collect this magic and bring it to me.\nThe satyrs dwell in northeastern Ashenvale because of the forest's power. They feed off its purity, leeching and corrupting. You can tell which satyrs have drawn the most of Ashenvale's magic by their swollen, uncloven hooves.\nThese hooves hold great power. I will need them for your gauntlets' crafting.","rew":"Experience: 1,200","back":"Do you have the hooves, ‹name›? The magic within them is strong.","done":"Ah, you have them! Now, just as the Satyrs leeched the strength of Ashenvale, I will leech the power held within these hooves and harness it into my crafting...","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":56.3,"y":74.3,"n":"Ula'elek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8402":{"id":8402,"t":"Fight for Warsong Gulch","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The Silverwing Sentinels are at war with the Warsong Outriders due to the destruction the Orcs are causing to the forest. There are, however, more reasons to defend this particular forest than plain love for nature.\nThe forest forms a strategic barrier that makes Ashenvale defendable against a large-scale attack. Without it, Astranaar would last a day or two before being annexed to the Barrens.\nDo your part in fighting the Warsong Outriders, ‹name›! For the Alliance!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","back":"You've come back with news from the front, ‹name›?","done":"Well done, ‹name›! You've served the Alliance well.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"4882":{"id":4882,"t":"Guarding Secrets","lv":59,"min":52,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Blue-feathered Necklace to Trull Failbane at Bloodvenom Post.\nBlue-feathered Necklace Berserk Owlbeast 50 % , Moontouched Owlbeast 50 % , Crazed Owlbeast 50 %\nProvided: Blue-feathered Necklace","desc":"You are unsure of the significance of the necklace that fell from the neck of the recently-slain wildkin. It glows brightly, slowly fading in and out.\nTrull Failbane might be able to tell you more, since his knowledge of the wildkin seems extensive. Perhaps you should ask him about it.","rew":"Experience: 3,200\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Reporting for another assignment?","done":"An important discovery?","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":34.7,"y":52.8,"n":"Trull Failbane","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"4802":{"id":4802,"t":"Winterfall E'ko","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Winterfall E'ko Winterfall Runner 20 % , High Chief Winterfall 20 % , Winterfall Pathfinder 20 % , Winterfall Totemic 20 % and 3 more","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Juju Power","back":"In Winterspring, you will fight misguided creatures known as da Winterfall furbolg. Through the wishes of their leader, dey have gained incredible strength. If you wish ta gain the power a' da Winterfall, bring me da E'ko you find from dem.\nRememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.","done":"Mau'ari can derive da juju for ‹name›... Use da Cache of Mau'ari to cast dis upon yourself or your allies.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Witch Doctor Mau'ari","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92642":{"id":92642,"t":"Disrupting logistics","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 4 Al'Aketh Healers and 8 Al'Aketh Brawlers in the Gustberry Lowlands.\nAl'Aketh Healer slain : 0/ 4\nAl'Aketh Brawler slain : 0/ 8","desc":"Valennia only sent one person to help repel a full-scale assault... by the winds.\nYou don't look like much but I'll take what I can get. We need to inflict as much damage as possible to stop this soon. My people can't hold out much longer.\nGo down the hill and disrupt their logistics. Their healers are keeping the attackers coming, if we take them out we might be able to rally and push them back. Any other cultists you kill while you are out there are helpful as well.","done":"You are still alive? Thank the winds for small miracles, I suppose.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":69.6,"y":67,"n":"Yorana Windyreed","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"3042":{"id":3042,"t":"Troll Temper","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Vials of Troll Temper to Trenton Lighthammer in Gadgetzan.\n20 Troll Temper Zerillis 55 % in Zul'Farrak , Dustwraith 55 % in Zul'Farrak , Sandarr Dunereaver 55 % in Zul'Farrak , Ruuzlu 55 % in Zul'Farrak and 4 more","desc":"The Sandfury trolls of Zul'Farrak make a tempering agent from sandstones, and I can use that to temper the goods I craft, yes I can! It is highly prized by connoisseurs, so if you bring me a good supply of the temper, then I'll reward you well.\nZul'Farrak is northwest of Gadgetzan. Good luck.","rew":"Money: 1 95 1 gold, 95 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900","back":"Did you bring me the temper, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, this is very nice temper indeed! And so much of it! I'll be at work for days before I use it all!\nThank you, ‹name›. Please, take this as payment.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.4,"y":28.8,"n":"Trenton Lighthammer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulfarrak"]}});